<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<% baseUrl="https://clipx.js.org/" %>
<% const esc = s => s.replace(/&/g,"&amp;").replace(/</g,"&lt;"); const code = (l, s) => '<pre class="code"><code class="language-'+l+'">'+esc(s)+'</code></pre>'; %>
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title><%= title %></title>
<link rel="shortcut icon" href="/favicon.ico" type="image/x-icon">
<meta name="description" content="ClipX JS is a tiny, dependency-free clipboard library: copy, cut, paste, text formatting and customizable toast notifications, driven by simple HTML data attributes. Try it in the live playground.">
<meta name="keywords" content="ClipX, ClipX JS, clipboard library, copy cut paste, JavaScript clipboard, toast notifications, clipboard API, text formatting, web development, developer toolkit">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light">
<meta name="robots" content="index, follow">
<meta property="og:title" content="ClipX JS — The Smarter Clipboard Solution">
<meta property="og:description" content="Copy, cut, paste and format text with HTML attributes. Built-in toast feedback and a live playground.">
<meta property="og:url" content="<%= baseUrl %>">
<meta property="og:image" content="<%= baseUrl %>images/banner.webp">
<meta property="og:image:alt" content="ClipX JS">
<meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
<meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
<meta property="og:site_name" content="ClipX JS">
<meta property="og:locale" content="en_US">
<link rel="canonical" href="<%= baseUrl %>">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/highlight.js/11.8.0/styles/atom-one-dark.min.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/stylesheets/styles.css">
</head>
<body>
<header class="top"><div class="wrap">
  <a class="logo" href="#top">Clip<b>X</b>.JS</a>
  <a class="l h" href="#playground">Playground</a><a class="l h" href="#install">Install</a><a class="l h" href="#attributes">Docs</a>
  <a class="l" href="https://github.com/mraxays/clipxjs" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a><span class="ver">v1.3.0</span>
</div></header>

<div class="wrap hero" id="top">
  <p class="eyebrow">MIT · zero dependencies · copy / cut / paste / format</p>
  <h1>The smarter clipboard solution.</h1>
  <p class="sub">Add clipboard actions and user feedback to any page using plain HTML attributes. Built-in toast notifications, text formatting, and nothing else to install.</p>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
    <a class="btn pri" href="#playground">Try the playground</a>
    <div class="pill"><code id="i-hero">npm i clipxjs</code><button class="btn" data-clipx-target="#i-hero" data-clipx-disable-msg data-clipx-msg="Copied">Copy</button></div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="wrap layout">
<aside>
  <a href="#playground">Playground</a><a href="#why">Why ClipX</a><a href="#install">Installation</a><a href="#start">Getting started</a><a href="#attributes">Attributes</a><a href="#formatting">Formatting</a><a href="#api">JavaScript API</a><a href="#events">Events</a><a href="#notes">Notes</a>
</aside>
<main>

<section id="playground">
  <h2>Playground</h2>
  <p>Change the options and use the live button. The code on the right updates as you go, and you can copy it straight into your project.</p>
  <div class="pg">
    <div class="ctrl">
      <div class="fld">Action<div class="seg"><button data-mode="text" class="on">Copy text</button><button data-mode="copy">Copy element</button><button data-mode="cut">Cut</button><button data-mode="paste">Paste</button></div></div>
      <label id="row-text">Text to copy<input class="in" id="in-text" value="  &lt;b&gt;Hello&lt;/b&gt;   from ClipX!  "></label>
      <div class="fld">Clean up (in click order)
        <div class="chips"><button data-f="striphtml">striphtml</button><button data-f="trim">trim</button><button data-f="collapse">collapse</button><button data-f="singleline">singleline</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="fld">Case (pick one)
        <div class="chips"><button data-f="uppercase">uppercase</button><button data-f="lowercase">lowercase</button><button data-f="capitalize">capitalize</button><button data-f="titlecase">titlecase</button></div>
      </div>
      <label>Message<input class="in" id="in-msg" placeholder="Copied!"></label>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2.5">
        <label>Position<select class="in" id="in-pos"><option>bottom</option><option>top</option></select></label>
        <label>Duration (ms)<input class="in" id="in-dur" type="number" value="1500" min="300" step="100"></label>
      </div>
      <label class="ck"><input type="checkbox" id="ck-only"> Toast only</label>
      <label class="ck"><input type="checkbox" id="ck-nomsg"> Keep button text</label>
      <label class="ck"><input type="checkbox" id="ck-notoast"> Disable toast</label>
    </div>
    <div class="out">
      <div class="prev" id="pg-prev"></div>
      <pre class="code" id="pg-code"><code class="language-html"></code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="why">
  <h2>Why ClipX.js?</h2>
  <p>A clipboard utility that handles the UI feedback too, so you don't need to wire up extra libraries or write the same handler in every project.</p>
  <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(230px,1fr))] gap-3.5">
    <div class="card"><b>Declarative</b><span>Behavior lives in your markup with <code>data-clipx-*</code> attributes. No custom event handlers.</span></div>
    <div class="card"><b>Built-in feedback</b><span>Customizable toasts and button messages, plus clear error toasts instead of silent failures.</span></div>
    <div class="card"><b>Copy, cut, paste, format</b><span>Clean text with chained formatters before it reaches the clipboard, or add your own.</span></div>
    <div class="card"><b>Easy integration</b><span>Event delegation means dynamically added buttons just work. Uses the Clipboard API with a copy fallback.</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="install">
  <h2>Installation</h2>
  <h3>NPM</h3>
  <%- code('bash', 'npm i clipxjs') %>
  <h3>CDN (use only one)</h3>
  <%- code('html', '<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/clipxjs/dist/clipx.min.js"></script>') %>
  <%- code('html', '<script src="https://unpkg.com/clipxjs/dist/clipx.min.js"></script>') %>
  <h3>Direct download</h3>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/mraxays/clipxjs/archive/refs/heads/main.zip" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Download the ZIP from GitHub</a></p>
</section>

<section id="start">
  <h2>Getting started</h2>
  <h3>Initialize</h3>
  <p><code>ClipX</code> is an alias of the <code>clipx</code> constructor, so naming your instance <code>clipx</code> doesn't shadow it.</p>
  <%- code('javascript', 'var clipx = new ClipX();\n\n// with a bundler\nconst ClipX = require("clipxjs");') %>
  <h3>Attach</h3>
  <p><code>attach()</code> uses event delegation, so it also works for elements added later, and it is safe to call more than once.</p>
  <%- code('javascript', 'clipx.attach(); // default: [data-clipx-text], [data-clipx-target], [data-clipx-paste]\nclipx.attach(".copy-btn, .your-class"); // custom selectors\nclipx.detach(); // remove all listeners') %>
  <h3>Configure</h3>
  <%- code('javascript', 'clipx.disable.msg = true;   // never change the element text\nclipx.disable.toast = true; // never show toasts\n\nclipx.setCustomStyles({\n  toast: "background:#333;color:#fff;padding:12px;border-radius:5px;", // all toasts\n  error: "background:#7a1f1f;"                                         // extra, for error toasts\n});') %>
  <p>Hide the toast icon with CSS:</p>
  <%- code('css', '.clipx-js-svg-icon { display: none; }') %>
</section>

<section id="attributes">
  <h2>Attributes</h2>
  <p>Add these to any element that matches your <code>attach()</code> selector. If several source attributes are present, the priority is <code>paste</code>, then <code>target</code>, then <code>text</code>.</p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto"><table>
    <tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Description</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-clipx-target</code></td><td>Selector of the element to copy (or cut) from. Inputs use their value; other elements their text.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-clipx-text</code></td><td>Static text to copy.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-clipx-paste</code></td><td>Selector of the element to paste into.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-clipx-cut</code></td><td>Clear the target after copying. Only works with <code>data-clipx-target</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-clipx-format</code></td><td>Comma-separated formatters applied before copy or paste: <code>trim</code>, <code>uppercase</code>, <code>lowercase</code>, <code>capitalize</code>, <code>titlecase</code>, <code>collapse</code>, <code>singleline</code>, <code>striphtml</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-clipx-msg</code></td><td>Custom success message (default <code>Copied!</code> / <code>Pasted!</code>).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-clipx-toast</code></td><td>Show only the toast; leave the element's text unchanged.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-clipx-disable-msg</code></td><td>Don't change the element's text.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-clipx-disable-toast</code></td><td>Don't show the toast.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-clipx-toast-position</code></td><td><code>top</code> or <code>bottom</code> (default).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-clipx-duration</code></td><td>Milliseconds the message stays visible (default <code>1500</code>).</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <h3>Examples</h3>
  <%- code('html', '<!-- copy from an element -->\n<p id="text-to-copy">This is the text to be copied.</p>\n<button data-clipx-target="#text-to-copy">Copy Text</button>\n\n<!-- static text with a custom message -->\n<button data-clipx-text="Static text" data-clipx-msg="Text copied successfully!">Copy</button>\n\n<!-- cut -->\n<textarea id="text-to-cut">This text will be cut.</textarea>\n<button data-clipx-target="#text-to-cut" data-clipx-cut>Cut</button>\n\n<!-- paste -->\n<textarea id="paste-here"></textarea>\n<button data-clipx-paste="#paste-here">Paste</button>\n\n<!-- toast only, on top, for 3 seconds -->\n<button data-clipx-text="Hi" data-clipx-toast data-clipx-toast-position="top" data-clipx-duration="3000">Copy</button>\n\n<!-- silent copy -->\n<button data-clipx-text="Hi" data-clipx-disable-toast data-clipx-disable-msg>Copy</button>') %>
</section>

<section id="formatting">
  <h2>Formatting</h2>
  <p>Formatters in <code>data-clipx-format</code> run left to right, before the text is copied or pasted. The case formatters (<code>uppercase</code>, <code>lowercase</code>, <code>capitalize</code>, <code>titlecase</code>) replace each other, so use only one of them per attribute.</p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto"><table>
    <tr><th>Formatter</th><th>Effect</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>trim</code></td><td>Remove leading and trailing whitespace</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>uppercase</code> / <code>lowercase</code></td><td>Change case</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>capitalize</code></td><td>Uppercase the first letter only</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>titlecase</code></td><td>Capitalize Each Word</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>collapse</code></td><td>Replace runs of whitespace with one space</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>singleline</code></td><td>Replace line breaks with a space</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>striphtml</code></td><td>Remove HTML tags (and script/style content) and decode entities, leaving plain text</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <%- code('javascript', '// add your own\nclipx.addFormatter("reverse", function (text) {\n  return text.split("").reverse().join("");\n});\n// <button data-clipx-text="abc" data-clipx-format="reverse">') %>
</section>

<section id="api">
  <h2>JavaScript API</h2>
  <p>Use ClipX without attributes. Copy, cut and paste methods return Promises.</p>
  <%- code('javascript', 'clipx.copyText("hello");                    // copy a string\nclipx.cutText("hello", element);            // copy, then clear element\nclipx.copyFromElement(element, "trim");     // optional format\nclipx.cutFromElement(element, "trim");\nclipx.pasteText();                          // resolves with clipboard text\nclipx.pasteToElement(element, "uppercase");\nclipx.format("  hi ", "trim,uppercase");    // sync, returns "HI"\nclipx.addFormatter(name, fn);\nclipx.attach(selector); clipx.detach();\nclipx.setCustomStyles({ toast, error });') %>
</section>

<section id="events">
  <h2>Events</h2>
  <p>ClipX dispatches bubbling events from the clicked element.</p>
  <%- code('javascript', 'document.addEventListener("clipx:success", function (e) {\n  console.log(e.target, e.detail.type); // "copy" | "cut" | "paste"\n});\n\ndocument.addEventListener("clipx:error", function (e) {\n  console.log(e.detail.error);\n});') %>
</section>

<section id="notes">
  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Works in modern browsers. Copy uses the Clipboard API and falls back to <code>execCommand("copy")</code> if it is unavailable or blocked.</li>
    <li>The Clipboard API requires a secure context (HTTPS or <code>localhost</code>).</li>
    <li><b>Paste</b> uses <code>navigator.clipboard.readText()</code>: it needs HTTPS, a user click, and usually a permission prompt. Support varies by browser, and an error toast shows when it isn't allowed.</li>
    <li>Cutting from a non-input element sets its text to empty, which removes any child elements inside it.</li>
    <li>Toast messages are inserted as plain text, so <code>data-clipx-msg</code> can't inject HTML.</li>
    <li>Upgrading from 1.2.x? The default message is now <code>Copied!</code>, and the old <code>isProcessing</code> property is gone.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

</main>
</div>

<footer><div class="wrap">
  <span>Made with ♥ by <a href="https://github.com/mraxays" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mr Akshay</a></span>
